  "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4-5x}x & <{3}^{2-5x}{x}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{4-5x}x-{3}^{2-5x}{x}^{2} & <0 \\\\ ({3}^{2}x-{x}^{2})\\cdot {3}^{2-5x} & <0 \\\\ (9x-{x}^{2})\\cdot {3}^{2-5x} & <0 \\\\ x(9-x)\\cdot {3}^{2-5x} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{2-5x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(9-x)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents a downwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=9.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when  $x<0$ or $x>9.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/assets/1c9e8e25c57c88476bedceea237fe78eb2a28d48008493f8609ac31d9aeda30b.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x<0$ or $x>9.$",
